# Smart Sea Belt System Architecture

The Smart Sea Belt is designed as an integrated marine safety system consisting of a wearable Smart Watch, Boat Hub, and Base Unit.

## System Architecture

```text
+----------------------+
|     SMART WATCH      |
|----------------------|
| ESP32-C3             |
| MAX30102             |
| MPU6050              |
| SOS Button           |
| GPS                  |
+----------+-----------+
           |
           | BLE
           v
+----------------------+
|      BOAT HUB        |
|----------------------|
| ESP32-S3             |
| BLE                  |
| GPS / NavIC          |
| LoRa                 |
| Emergency Processing |
+----------+-----------+
           |
           | LoRa
           v
+----------------------+
|      BASE UNIT       |
|----------------------|
| Controller           |
| LoRa Receiver       |
| Display / Alerts     |
+----------+-----------+
           |
           v
   Monitoring Platform
```

## 1. Smart Watch

The Smart Watch is the wearable safety unit.

It collects:

- Heart-rate information
- Motion information
- Location information
- SOS status

The ESP32-C3 processes the sensor information and communicates with the Boat Hub through Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE).

## 2. Boat Hub

The Boat Hub acts as the central communication and processing unit on the boat.

It:

- Receives Smart Watch information
- Processes emergency information
- Monitors boat location
- Communicates with the Base Unit using LoRa
- Provides an interface for the rudder mechanism

## 3. Base Unit

The Base Unit receives information from the Boat Hub through LoRa.

It is responsible for:

- Receiving safety information
- Processing emergency messages
- Providing local alerts
- Displaying monitoring information
- Supporting future cloud connectivity

